<title>FRANCE: Club Med extends gains on bid rumours.</title>
<headline>Club Med extends gains on bid rumours.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Club Mediterranee was up nearly three percent, extending its gains on market rumours that hotel group Accor could launch a bid for the travel company.</p>
<p>At 1055 GMT, the company was up 2.80 percent or 9.0 francs at 330.0. On Wednesday, Club Med gained 3.98 percent.</p>
<p>Both companies have declined comment on the rumours.</p>
<p>Analysts have said a takeover offer by Accor would make little sense industrially and would run counter to Accor's aim of cutting its debt. They see a foreign company as a more likely target than Club Med.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
